### StayFinder API smoke tests
### VS Code extension: REST Client
### Start backend at http://localhost:4000 before running.
### Replace the IDs and cookie below with values from YOUR local test database/session.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:4000
@cookie = REPLACE_WITH_AUTH_SESSION_COOKIE
@propertyId = REPLACE_WITH_EXISTING_PUBLISHED_PROPERTY_UUID
@ownedPropertyId = REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_OWN_PROPERTY_UUID
@missingPropertyId = 00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000
@bookingId = REPLACE_WITH_BOOKING_UUID

### 1. PUBLIC: list published properties — expected 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/properties

### 2. PUBLIC: filter properties — expected 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/properties?city=Stockholm&guests=2&maxPrice=2000

### 3. PUBLIC: property details — expected 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/properties/{{propertyId}}

### 4. INVALID UUID — expected 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/properties/not-a-uuid

### 5. VALID UUID, missing property — expected 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/properties/{{missingPropertyId}}

### 6. AUTH REQUIRED: list my properties while logged out — expected 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/properties/mine

### 7. AUTH REQUIRED: list bookings while logged out — expected 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/bookings

### 8. CREATE PROPERTY while logged in — expected 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/properties
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: {{cookie}}

{
  "title": "API Test Apartment",
  "description": "A test property created through the API.",
  "city": "Stockholm",
  "country": "Sweden",
  "address": "Test Street 1",
  "price_per_night": 1200,
  "max_guests": 2,
  "images": [],
  "is_published": true
}

### 9. INVALID PROPERTY BODY — expected 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/properties
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: {{cookie}}

{
  "title": "",
  "description": "Invalid test data",
  "city": "Stockholm",
  "country": "Sweden",
  "address": "Test Street 1",
  "price_per_night": -10,
  "max_guests": 0,
  "images": [],
  "is_published": true
}

### 10. MALFORMED JSON — expected 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/properties
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: {{cookie}}

{ "title": "Broken JSON",

### 11. CREATE BOOKING while logged in — expected 201
### Use a published property that is not owned by the logged-in user.
POST {{baseUrl}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: {{cookie}}

{
  "property_id": "{{propertyId}}",
  "guest_name": "API Test Guest",
  "guest_email": "api-test@example.com",
  "check_in": "2027-06-10",
  "check_out": "2027-06-13",
  "guests": 2
}

### 12. INVALID BOOKING — expected 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: {{cookie}}

{
  "property_id": "not-a-uuid",
  "guest_name": "A",
  "guest_email": "not-an-email",
  "check_in": "not-a-date",
  "check_out": "2027-06-10",
  "guests": 0
}

### 13. UPDATE OWN PROPERTY — expected 200
### Use a property owned by the authenticated user.
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/properties/{{ownedPropertyId}}
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: {{cookie}}

{
  "title": "Updated API Test Apartment"
}

### 14. UPDATE PROPERTY NOT OWNED BY USER — expected 403
### propertyId must belong to another user.
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/properties/{{propertyId}}
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: {{cookie}}

{
  "title": "Attempted unauthorized update"
}

### 15. INVALID BOOKING ID — expected 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/bookings/not-a-uuid
Cookie: {{cookie}}

### 16. GET MY BOOKINGS while logged in — expected 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/bookings?limit=100
Cookie: {{cookie}}

### 17. DELETE PROPERTY WITH EXISTING BOOKINGS — expected 409
### Only run if ownedPropertyId has at least one booking and the API prevents deletion.
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/properties/{{ownedPropertyId}}
Cookie: {{cookie}}

### Notes
# - Some route implementations may use a different response body shape; the status code is the primary assertion here.
# - If your app's route prefix or query parameter names differ, adjust the request to match the actual route files.
# - Do not run destructive requests against real or production data.
# - Cookie-based auth may require the exact cookie name/value from browser DevTools.
